        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: South Cheshire Way, Cheshire, West Midlands, Grindley Brook, Whitchurch, Mow Cop, Cheshire-Staffordshire border\n- Topics: long-distance footpaths, route sections, regional geography\n\nFacts:\n- The South Cheshire Way is a 32-mile long-distance footpath.\n- The South Cheshire Way runs east-west mainly through Cheshire and the West Midlands.\n- The western section of the South Cheshire Way starts at Grindley Brook near Whitchurch and runs through farmland.\n- The eastern section of the South Cheshire Way starts from the isolated village of Mow Cop and straddles the Cheshire-Staffordshire border.\n- The eastern section of the South Cheshire Way is divided between the North West and West Midlands regions.",
